{"type":"standard","title":"Larry Rhoden","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Larry Rhoden</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16193325","titles":{"canonical":"Larry_Rhoden","normalized":"Larry Rhoden","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Larry Rhoden</span></span>"},"pageid":40258673,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Larry_Rhoden_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Larry_Rhoden_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":470},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Larry_Rhoden_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2014,"height":2867},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1380547434","tid":"7c997d17-c956-11f1-99c8-c626266b8649","timestamp":"2026-10-16T11:41:12Z","description":"Governor of South Dakota since 2025","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Larry_Rhoden"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Larry_Rhoden","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Larry_Rhoden"}},"extract":"Larry Robert Rhoden is an American politician and businessman serving since 2025 as the 34th governor of South Dakota. A member of the Republican Party, Rhoden served from 2019 to 2025 as the 39th Lieutenant Governor of South Dakota and from 2009 to 2015 and again from 2017 until 2019 in the South Dakota Legislature.","extract_html":"<p><b>Larry Robert Rhoden</b> is an American politician and businessman serving since 2025 as the 34th governor of South Dakota. A member of the Republican Party, Rhoden served from 2019 to 2025 as the 39th Lieutenant Governor of South Dakota and from 2009 to 2015 and again from 2017 until 2019 in the South Dakota Legislature.</p>"}